    "body": {
      "type": "doc",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The Aga Khan University (AKU)'s Department of Anaesthesiology in collaboration with the Department of Continuing Professional Education (at AKU), Committee for European Education in Anaesthesiology (CEEA, which is affiliated with European Society of Anaesthesiologists), and World Federation of Societies of Anaesthesiologists (WFSA), successfully organized the CEEA Continuing Medical Education course titled 'Heart and Circulation' from March 20-22, 2015."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The programme aimed to maintain and raise the standards of anaesthetic care at the highest possible level through continuing medical education in anaesthesiology. The course included interactive lectures, case based discussions, hands-on workshops on Ultrasound-guided Vascular Access, Cardiopulmonary Resuscitation and Echocardiography. The course was attended by consultants and anaesthesia trainees from AKU and other teaching hospitals of Karachi, Hyderabad, and Nawabshah."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
